# assistente utile U12 (docs/plans/assistente-utile.md) — una quantita' per
# periodo, per quanti periodi: tre pezzi del turno e la conversione della durata
# con quantity/3, tutto in KB (numeric-questions.p0 §4).
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test a monthly saving over years converts the duration]
!timeout 30
> If I save 50 euros a month, how much will I have in two years?
< 1200 euros.

[test the same over months, and a daily cost over weeks]
!timeout 30
> I save 50 euros every month. How much do I save in 24 months?
< 1200 euros.
> I spend 3 euros a day on coffee. How much do I spend in 2 weeks?
< 42 euros.

[test mix 13x08 a quantity per thing, times the number of things asked]
!timeout 30
> how many legs do three spiders have?
< 24 legs: 3 spiders with 8 legs each.
> how many days are in two weeks?
< 14 days: 2 weeks with 7 days each.
> how many legs does a spider have?
<~ 8 legs

[test mix 13x15 power, hours and price have roles, not a bag of numbers]
!timeout 30
> how much does it cost to run a 2000 watt heater for 3 hours at 0.25 euros per kwh?
< 1.5 euros: 6 kWh at 0.25 per kWh.
> how many kwh does a 2000 watt heater use in 3 hours?
< 6 kWh: 2000 watts for 3 hours.
<! 1997

[test mix 16x14x13 backward planning from a time, with durations read by position]
!timeout 30
> if the roast needs 90 minutes and dinner is at 8 pm, when should I start cooking?
< 18:30
> the meeting is at 9 am and the drive takes 1 hour 20 minutes, when should I leave?
< 07:40
> my train leaves at 7:45 and it takes 25 minutes to walk to the station, when should I leave?
< 07:20

[test mix 15x13 the cheaper pack is decided per kilo or per liter]
!timeout 30
> which is cheaper: 750 g for 3 euros or 1 kg for 3.80 euros?
< 1 kg for 3.80 is cheaper: 3.8 per kilo against 4 per kilo.
> which is the better deal, 500 ml for 2 euros or 1.5 liters for 5 euros?
< 1.5 liters for 5 is cheaper: 3.33 per liter against 4 per liter.

[test mix 08x16x14 a bedtime window from the wake time and the taught sleep need]
!timeout 30
> I wake up at 6:30, when should I go to bed?
< Between 21:30 and 23:30: adults need 7 to 9 hours of sleep.
> I wake up at 7:00 and want 8 hours of sleep, when should I go to bed?
< 23:00

[test mix 13x08 cups to grams depend on the ingredient]
!timeout 30
> how many grams are 2 cups of flour?
< 240 grams: a cup of flour weighs 120 grams.
> how many grams is half a cup of sugar?
< 99 grams: a cup of sugar weighs 198 grams.
> how many grams are 2 cups of sand?
<! grams:

[test mix 13x15x12 a measurement against the taught recommended range]
!timeout 30
> the humidity in my bedroom is 70 percent, is that a problem?
< That is high: indoor humidity should stay between 30 and 50 percent, and 70 is above that. High humidity causes mold.
> my hygrometer says the humidity is 45 percent
< That is fine: 45 percent is inside the recommended 30 to 50 percent for indoor humidity.
